<title>USA: Mark IV sees Q4 gain from $17 mln sale.</title>
<headline>Mark IV sees Q4 gain from $17 mln sale.</headline>
<dateline>AMHERST, N.Y. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mark IV Industries Inc said Thursday that it will realize a fourth quarter gain from the sale of its Automatic Signal/Eagle Signal unit to Siemens Energy &amp; Automation Inc for $17 million cash.</p>
<p>The unit makes traffic signals and controllers and had revenue of $27.6 million in the fiscal year ended February 29, 1996.</p>
<p>The company said the sale brings aggregate proceeds from its divestiture program in fiscal 1997 to about $271 million.</p>
<p>Siemens Energy &amp; Automation Inc is part of Siemens AG.</p>
</text>
